---
import { RELEASES_URL } from '../lib/releases';

const repoUrl = RELEASES_URL.replace(/\/releases$/, '');
---

<footer class="site-footer">
  <div class="wrap cols">
    <p class="story">
      <strong>Why “Lontar”?</strong> Lontar are the palm-leaf manuscripts once used in Bali and Java to
      record knowledge, one carefully written row at a time.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/download">Download</a></li>
      <li><a href={repoUrl}>Source code</a></li>
      <li><a href={`${repoUrl}/issues`}>Report a problem</a></li>
      <li><a href={`${repoUrl}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>Apache-2.0 license</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap fine">
    <p>
      Lontar is free and open-source software. PostgreSQL, MySQL, MariaDB and SQLite are trademarks of their
      respective owners.
    </p>
  </div>
</footer>

<style>
  .site-footer {
    margin-top: clamp(4rem, 10vw, 7rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding: 2.5rem 0 2rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
  .cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 2rem;
  }
  .story strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }
  .fine p {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .cols {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
